  "prefLabel": "Cul-H 102.20 Inventory form",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cul-H 102.20 “Inventory form” means a form used to record and understand the appearance, history, and significance of a building, structure, site, district, area, landscape, or object prior to listing on the state or National Registers of Historic Places, for a historic resources survey or planning project, or for review and compliance purposes. “Inventory form” includes an area form, individual inventory form, and an archaeological inventory form.\n\nSource. #10217, eff 10-30-12, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cul-h100.html"
